OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Settings/**`.
That path does NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group. The repo's
real, compiled canonical page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/` (the shipped
Admin / Maps / Dashboard pages live there; `Sources` is a project.yml source path with
createIntermediateGroups). Page hosting uses the proven SettingsRouteRegistration /
ApiPlaygroundRouteRegistration pattern. The page therefore ships at
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Settings/**` — the faithful equivalent of the prompt's
`Features/Settings`; tests at `apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Settings/`; strings in the
platform catalog `apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This
mapping is the only deviation from the literal prompt path and is recorded here per covenant #9.
Gate commands below were run against the REAL paths.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY APPROACH (web HelixPage is a PageContainer wrapper over <AISettings />)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web page is a thin `PageContainer` (title + subtitle + `Integrations › Helix` breadcrumb,
`loading={useSettings().isLoading}`) whose sole child is the `<AISettings />` configuration
surface. The native `AISettings` surface ALREADY EXISTS at parity
(apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/AISettings*.swift, driven by AiSettingsModel). This unit
therefore ships the PAGE: the breadcrumb + page title/subtitle chrome (always rendered), the
`useSettings → GET /settings` page-level query state holder, every data state, and it HOSTS the
existing AISettings surface on success — exactly the web composition. No AISettings logic is
duplicated.

